A||||4||mrfiero||wiring questions||||1||
Z||000000||mrfiero||12-31-2000||03:00 AM||||I have a friend of mine doing an engine swap (4.9 caddy) and ran into a couple of snags.  The donor car is an '88 coupe 2.5 5-sp. (will be an auto.).<P>#1  What does terminal "D" on the ALDL do?  I think it is the fuel pump, but I need to make sure.<P>#2 Where do the DIS engines get the signal for the tach to work?<P>#3 Shoot....I forgot!  It had something to do with the AC compressor.  I'll have to call him up to find out what his question was.<P><BR>Any help on the first 2 questions would be appreciated.  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||12-31-2000||06:25 PM||||? # 1) Pin 'D' would be for the check engine light, pin 'G' (if used) would be the fuel pump. (I think this is correct)<P>? # 2) Tach reference is off pin 'A' of the ignition module.<P>? # 3) Beats me!(LOL)||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||12-31-2000||08:44 PM||||Pin D of the ALDL is the link for a scanner. 160 buad. It uses the CE/SES lamp output to transmit the data (which is why the light flashes).<P>What pin of the ALDL does the 4.9L use? If it uses E (Serial 160) or M (Serial 8192) you want to use that wire or no scanner will be able to communicate with it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||12-31-2000||09:00 PM||||The 1227748 DIS ECM also contains the cruise control module so if this car had cruise it's dead now. You'll have to go to an aftermarket system.<P>This guy has a pinout online that covers all the terminals. <A HREF="http://www.euronet.nl/users/fo_elmo/fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.euronet.nl/users/fo_elmo/fiero.htm</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfiero||12-31-2000||11:31 PM||||Thanks for the replies......I appreciate it.  I have no idea what pin the 4.9 uses, but at least I now know what the Fieros pin D is for.<P>I'm not sure if he plans on using cruise, but I will relay that info to him.<P><BR>I still need to figure out where the tach info comes from on the DIS motors.....anyone??<P>Thanks again......I'll give him this info and I'll ask what his AC question was too.<BR> ||||reg||10
